gone for the new systems sorry  2k15 features the current raw Smackdown  rosters a handful of NXT superstars and  a similarly limited selection of classic  performers the entire create X modes  have been removed from the game  including create a diva create a  storyline create a finisher and more  it's a shame that the stories and  personalities that keep audiences tuned  into wrestling every week are so absent  from my career mode because the series  has never looked better new technology  and a new console generation of led to  night and day leaps forward in terms of  character capture stars like Dolph  Ziggler Randy Orton Sami Zayn many more  stunning with animations that even  managed to capture some of the signature  facial tics not all the character models  are success though superstars with  pronounced facial features become  cartoonish in this new technology and  many characters what large foreheads  seem comically micro proportion in this  game that's nothing compared to  characters with large mouths though such  as the Mazur summer-rae who become  almost monstrous with freaky distended  smiles the in-ring combat is seen nearly  as much of an improvement as the game's  visuals though the new collar-and-elbow  tie-up system for the beginning of  matches adds an interesting strategic  tweak it's the new stamina and health  systems that will totally revamp how you  play WWE 2k15 each character has a  stamina bar and three health bars if you  lose a health bar you drop down to the  equivalent stamina bar if you haven't  fallen there already that ensures that  if you're low at health your character  is now beat to hell and completely worn  out he or she can't move as quickly as  they did at the beginning of the match  which slows their and paced  significantly but also makes matches  more realistic certain wrinkles of  combat are still problematic counters  still refuse to become an intuitive  process - countering attacks it's too  easy to lose all your first stamina bar  if you're at the losing end of the  rock-paper-scissors element of the  collar and elbow tie ups and reversals  do such a disproportionate amount of  damage that it really creates a  disincentive to perform many moves in  your arsenal furthermore though they're  much rarer than we see in the last gen  versions bugs still pop up WWE 2k15  feels much like the modern WWE it is  capable of delivering great in-ring  action and it has the flashy production  values that none of its competitors can  match but it's hard to care about  anything that's happening beyond the  moment-to-moment competition at no point  does WWE 2k15  Janan to something truly special  you're  we'll see you next time
 

